From 733df21365e0506ac205bbc98b68f5e4f120705d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Noa Himesaka <himesaka@noa.codes>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 15:27:11 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 87/94] cpufreq: qcom-hw: Vote the bandwidth of the starting
 frequency

With an OPP table in DT the driver votes each OPP's interconnect
bandwidth from ->target_index(). The cpufreq core does not call that
for the frequency a policy already runs at: __cpufreq_driver_target()
returns early when the target equals policy->cur. So a policy whose
governor asks for the frequency the OSM already runs at, and keeps
asking for it, never votes at all: the performance governor on a
cluster that is already at its top frequency, or schedutil under
steady full load.

Vote the bandwidth of the frequency the OSM runs at once the OPPs are
in place, as the downstream devfreq-cpufreq governor does with the
policy's current frequency when the policy appears.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01SXjPGasJxD6XRYU1J9jsnW
---
 drivers/cpufreq/qcom-cpufreq-hw.c | 15 +++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 15 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/cpufreq/qcom-cpufreq-hw.c b/drivers/cpufreq/qcom-cpufreq-hw.c
index 58222a11b..d4a2594e7 100644
--- a/drivers/cpufreq/qcom-cpufreq-hw.c
+++ b/drivers/cpufreq/qcom-cpufreq-hw.c
@@ -1832,6 +1832,21 @@ static int qcom_cpufreq_hw_cpu_init(struct cpufreq_policy *policy)
 		return -ENODEV;
 	}
 
+	/*
+	 * The bandwidth is only voted from ->target_index(), and the core
+	 * skips that for the frequency the policy already runs at.  Vote it
+	 * for the starting frequency here, or a policy that stays there
+	 * (e.g. under the performance governor) never asks for any.
+	 */
+	if (icc_scaling_enabled) {
+		unsigned int freq = qcom_cpufreq_get_freq(policy);
+
+		ret = qcom_cpufreq_set_bw(policy, freq);
+		if (ret)
+			dev_warn(cpu_dev, "Failed to set bandwidth for %u kHz: %d\n",
+				 freq, ret);
+	}
+
 	return qcom_cpufreq_hw_lmh_init(policy, index);
 }
 
